# FLOODCAST (SIH26085) — required external credentials
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in only the values you actually have.
# NEVER commit a real `.env` file. Scripts read these via environment
# variables (e.g. python-dotenv or your shell), never hard-coded.
#
# Every variable below is genuinely required by a specific data-acquisition
# script — see the "Why" comment above each one. If a variable is left
# blank, the corresponding script documents the dataset as UNAVAILABLE /
# REQUIRES API KEY rather than fabricating data.

# --- Rainfall (JAXA GSMaP FTP) ---
# Why: data/raw/rainfall/scripts/download_gsmap.py needs FTP login to
# ftp.ptree.jaxa.jp to fetch additional GSMaP Gauge hourly files (e.g. to
# pull a date range that actually contains a rain event, since the currently
# downloaded 2026-09-06 window is dry). Free registration at
# https://sharaku.eorc.jaxa.jp/register/
JAXA_FTP_USER=
JAXA_FTP_PASSWORD=

# --- DEM (Copernicus DEM GLO-30 via OpenTopography) ---
# Why: data/scripts/download_dem.py needs this to fetch elevation data for
# Greater Mumbai. Without it, DEM, slope, flow accumulation, and all
# DEM-derived (INFERRED) surface drainage remain unavailable. Free account +
# API key at https://opentopography.org/ (myOpenTopo -> Request API key).
OPENTOPOGRAPHY_API_KEY=

# --- IMD API (rainfall / nowcast) ---
# Why: IMD's public API (api.imd.gov.in) is IP-whitelist / registration
# gated per the verified data-source sheet. Not currently integrated into
# any script because access could not be confirmed — set this and update
# data/scripts/ if/when access is granted.
IMD_API_KEY=

# --- Sentinel-1 flood-extent validation ---
# Why: data/scripts/download_validation.py's Sentinel-1 step needs one of
# these to run actual change-detection validation against a historical
# Mumbai flood event. Free accounts at
# https://dataspace.copernicus.eu/ (username/password) or
# https://earthengine.google.com/ (service-account JSON key path).
COPERNICUS_DATASPACE_USER=
COPERNICUS_DATASPACE_PASSWORD=
GEE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON=

# --- MCGM AWS/ARG 15-minute rain gauges ---
# Why: dm.mcgm.gov.in/aws has no documented public JSON API (confirmed in
# the verified data-source sheet — scraping is fragile/TOS-uncertain). If
# MCGM's Disaster Management Unit grants a formal API/data-sharing
# agreement, its access token would go here.
MCGM_AWS_API_TOKEN=
